From: Reinhard Tartler <siretart@tauware.de>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:01:40 +0200
Subject: skip-flaky-maintenance-test.patch

Skip flaky TestSilences_Maintenance_SupportsCustomCallback on slow
architectures (like armhf) due to race condition between starting the
maintenance goroutine and advancing the mock mock clock.

Upstream is replacing the clock mock entirely with testing/synctest:
https://github.com/prometheus/alertmanager/pull/5376
https://github.com/prometheus/alertmanager/pull/5394

Forwarded: not-needed
---
 silence/silence_test.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/silence/silence_test.go b/silence/silence_test.go
index c083044..9aacec8 100644
--- a/silence/silence_test.go
+++ b/silence/silence_test.go
@@ -559,6 +559,7 @@ func TestSilences_Maintenance_DefaultMaintenanceFuncDoesntCrash(t *testing.T) {
 }
 
 func TestSilences_Maintenance_SupportsCustomCallback(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Skip("Skip flaky test on architectures with slow goroutine orchestration. See upstream issues #5376, #5394")
 	f, err := os.CreateTemp(t.TempDir(), "snapshot")
 	require.NoError(t, err, "creating temp file failed")
 	clock := quartz.NewMock(t)
